second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"When was Judge Howe born?\", \"slot_hint\": \"birth_date\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 113, \"text\": \"Harland Bradley Howe Harland Bradley Howe (February 19, 1873 – April 22, 1946) was a United States federal judge.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d00\", \"start\": 114, \"end\": 134, \"text\": \"Howe was born in St.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d00\", \"start\": 135, \"end\": 199, \"text\": \"Johnsbury, Vermont on February 19, 1873, the son of Worcester C.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d00\", \"start\": 200, \"end\": 233, \"text\": \"Howe and Rosaline (Bradley) Howe.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d00\", \"start\": 234, \"end\": 307, \"text\": \"He was educated in Caledonia County, and graduated from Lyndon Institute.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d00\", \"start\": 308, \"end\": 430, \"text\": \"Originally trained as a harness maker, he contracted polio which left him unable to perform such demanding physical labor.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d00\", \"start\": 431, \"end\": 557, \"text\": \"He began to study law with an attorney in Lyndonville, Vermont, and afterwards attended the University of Michigan Law School.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d00\", \"start\": 558, \"end\": 617, \"text\": \"Unable to continue his studies after the first year because\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 88, \"text\": \"Harland Bradley Howe (July 15, 1875 – April 22, 1946) was a United States federal judge.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d01\", \"start\": 89, \"end\": 109, \"text\": \"Howe was born in St.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d01\", \"start\": 110, \"end\": 170, \"text\": \"Johnsbury, Vermont on July 15, 1875, the son of Worcester C.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d01\", \"start\": 171, \"end\": 204, \"text\": \"Howe and Rosaline (Bradley) Howe.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d01\", \"start\": 205, \"end\": 278, \"text\": \"He was educated in Caledonia County, and graduated from Lyndon Institute.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d01\", \"start\": 279, \"end\": 401, \"text\": \"Originally trained as a harness maker, he contracted polio which left him unable to perform such demanding physical labor.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d01\", \"start\": 402, \"end\": 528, \"text\": \"He began to study law with an attorney in Lyndonville, Vermont, and afterwards attended the University of Michigan Law School.\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d01\", \"start\": 529, \"end\": 663, \"text\": \"Unable to continue his studies after the first year because of financial constraints, he returned to Vermont and began practicing law.\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 131, \"text\": \"James Henry Howe James Henry Howe (December 5, 1827 – January 4, 1893) was known for his position as a United States federal judge.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d02\", \"start\": 132, \"end\": 220, \"text\": \"Born in Turner, Maine, Howe began to study law in 1848 with his uncle Timothy Otis Howe.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d02\", \"start\": 221, \"end\": 361, \"text\": \"During his lifetime, he operated a private law firm, served in the army as a Colonel, and was appointed to be a United States federal judge.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d02\", \"start\": 362, \"end\": 538, \"text\": \"He was the Attorney General of Wisconsin from 1860 to 1862, preceding his service in the United States Army in the 32nd Wisconsin Volunteer Infantry Regiment from 1862 to 1864.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d02\", \"start\": 539, \"end\": 553, \"text\": \"Howe worked at\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 87, \"text\": \"James Henry Howe | Military Wiki | Fandom Start a Wiki Sign In Do n't have an account ?\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d03\", \"start\": 88, \"end\": 503, \"text\": \"Register Sign In Military Wiki Explore Main Page Discuss All Pages Community Interactive Maps Popular pages Most visited articles Military ranks of the Philippines List of currently active United States military land vehicles Project maintenance Double redirects Broken redirects Wanted categories Wanted pages Wanted templates Uncategorized Categories Short pages Unused categories Sign In Do n't have an account ?\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d03\", \"start\": 504, \"end\": 650, \"text\": \"Register Sign In Explore Fan Central Current Skip to content Military 353,117 pages Explore Main Page Discuss All Pages Community Interactive Maps\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0137-10a83e10786d:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Judge Howe\", 